<title>CHINA: Shanghai, Beijing ban new beeper exchange stations.</title>
<headline>Shanghai, Beijing ban new beeper exchange stations.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai and Beijing have banned new beeper exchange stations because too many were already in operation, the Shanghai-based Business News said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>At end-1996, China had about 2,700 beeper exchange stations, occupying nearly 10,000 frequencies, the newspaper said, adding that 90 percent capacity of the capacity was being wasted.</p>
</text>
